WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.920
[UPBEAT MUSIC]

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:04.640
 Write your truth,
and believe in it.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.335
And if your mother
doesn't like it, too bad.

00:00:07.335 --> 00:00:09.660
[LAUGHS]

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:12.810
The novel is creating
a whole new mode

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.580
of understanding the world.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.160
Over the last 30 years
of being a novelist,

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.770
I've learned how
that's worked, and I've

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.400
made a commitment to it.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.750
And I would love to talk to
you about that commitment.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.180
I'm going to talk
to you about how

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:31.050
to choose the right
words, structure, story,

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:35.280
characters to create
the novel that's in you.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.550
The Black male heroes are the
major characters in my novels

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:40.470
because there have
been very few novels

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.960
written about Black male heroes.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.350
If you want to be in the
history of the culture,

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:49.650
then you have to
exist in the fiction.

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.930
If you don't exist
in the literature,

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:54.280
your people don't exist.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:57.180
I wake up, write three
hours, 1,000 words.

00:00:57.180 --> 00:01:00.360
Next day, the first thing I
do is reread that 1,000 words

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.890
I wrote yesterday.

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:03.840
And then I write my
next 1,000 words.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.890
And that goes on and on until
I get to the end of the novel.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:10.830
If you write every
day, the next day,

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:13.140
ideas have bubbled
up from some place

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.300
that you had no idea were there.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.310
One of the great
things about starting

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:21.510
writing for me at the age
of 34 was that I was already

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:23.480
a failure in life.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:29.880
In failing, you can find out
the right way of doing things.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:32.980
A lot of you will be
intimidated to start writing.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.900
Throw all that fear
out the window.

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.170
It doesn't matter,
'cause it doesn't.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:40.200
The only thing I need you
to leave this class with

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.610
is the confidence that
you can write a novel.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:46.500
You will write that novel.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.570
I couldn't ask
for anything more.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:54.330
I'm Walter Mosley, and
this is my MasterClass.

